    Archive a replaced agent's unsafe hold on every Act 19 reset path
    
    The independent review of the integration candidate found that threshold
    resets in branch-bootstrap.sh, clerk-liveness.sh and seat-liveness.sh replace
    the agent without archiving its stale unsafe-hold line, so an office could stay
    blocked after a lawful reset. terminal-continuity.sh did archive, but with a
    blind mv that also moved other invocations' holds and could overwrite earlier
    evidence.
    
    Add one shared POSIX helper, oc_archive_hold, that moves only the lines whose
    tab-separated agent id matches the replaced agent, keeps unrelated holds, uses
    a non-colliding archive name, and is idempotent. Call it on all four replace
    paths. Archiving failure is reported but does not block recovery; the hold
    stays in place as evidence.
    
    Regression coverage: the threshold-reset fixture now plants a stale hold and
    asserts it is archived and removed; a unit block asserts another agent's hold
    survives, a repeated archive does not duplicate, and an emptied hold file is
    deleted. Focused appointment, continuity, institutional, branch-health and
    Act 19 tests pass.

